Schema disclosure: Workflow tool_input shape is SCHEMA-DOC-DERIVED, not captured live.

Pins Stage 2 reviewer Bug C (false positive -- the worst of the three, a correctly pinned call getting DENIED): the opts object passed to agent( carries a nested call argument, onEvent: cb({ x: 1 }), BEFORE the model: key. That nested argument's own closing sequence "})" (the '}' closing its object literal immediately followed by the ')' closing cb(...)) is textually indistinguishable from the outer agent( call's own closing "})" under a scanner that treats the literal two-character substring "})" as the block terminator -- so a line-buffered scanner that appends whole lines and checks for that substring closes the block after the onEvent line, before ever appending the model: line, and denies a call that IS pinned.

The correct contract tracks PARENTHESIS depth character-by-character from the agent( call's own opening "(": nested "(" / ")" pairs (including the cb(...) argument, whatever curly braces appear inside it) only affect depth, they do not terminate the block early. The block ends only when depth returns to 0 at the call's own closing paren -- which in this fixture comes AFTER model: "sonnet". Expected result: exit 0, stdout byte-for-byte EMPTY (allow) -- not a deny.
